# Way of work

When the user asks for a feature or behavior change, follow the `way-of-work` skill before writing production code.

## When it applies

- New features or behavior changes
- Bug fixes that change observable behavior
- Refactors that should preserve behavior (write/extend tests first)

## When to skip

- Questions, reviews, investigations, or docs-only requests
- Pure config/tooling with no behavior under test
- Explicit user instruction to skip the loop (e.g. "just commit", "quick fix")

## Companion skills

- Planning slices: `way-of-planning`
- Test quality: `smelly-test`
- Post-green cleanup: `rules-of-refactoring`
